    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d667-a1">

                <pb facs="1071" n="935" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg935"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 217.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Piquant to Mr.
                            Thompson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State of Foreign Relations, Section No.</hi> —
                                —,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1888-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 22, 1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to inform you
                    that the steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Haytian Republic</hi> having been
                    captured for having forced the blockade before St. Marc, a tribunal bas been
                    formed so that the affair be submitted to its appreciation.</p>
                <p>I hasten to give you notice in the mean time, that it be permitted me to submit
                    to you the verdict of that tribunal in the circumstance.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.</p>
                <p>The counselor of the interior, charged per interim with the department of state
                    of foreign relations,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O.
                        Piquant</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
